course: dictionary
lesson: 14256
title: Netted: caught, scored or earned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Netted is a good example. It comes from the word net, and it is the past tense of net. «The fisherman netted six fish before lunch.» Here netted means caught with a net.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence to choose the right meaning. «Sam netted twice in the second half.» In football, netted means scored a goal, because the ball goes into the net. «The shop netted £500 after paying all its costs.» With money, netted means the profit left over after the costs are paid.
explain: Netted can also be an adjective, meaning covered with a net or a pattern like a net. «The apples were kept in a netted bag.» Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Net, nets, netted and netting are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Netted» means caught with a net, as in «the fisherman netted fish».
fact: In sport, «netted» means scored, especially a goal in football or hockey.
fact: With money, «netted» means earned as profit after costs, as in «netted £500».
fact: As an adjective, «netted» means covered with a net or a pattern like a net.
exercise: «The fisherman netted six fish before lunch.» What does netted mean here? | Sold at the harbour market | *Caught with a net | Cooked in a hot pan | Thrown back into the sea
exercise: «Sam netted twice in the second half.» What does netted mean in this sentence? | Lost the ball | *Scored goals | Ran very fast | Kicked the ball out of play
exercise: Mum netted the strawberry bushes to keep the birds off. What does netted mean here? | Planted in a neat row | Picked clean of fruit | *Covered with a net | Watered every morning
test: «The shop netted £500 after paying all its costs.» What does netted mean here? | Lost in a storm | *Earned as profit after costs | Spent on new shelves | Given away to charity
test: «The apples were kept safe in a netted bag.» What does netted mean here? | *Covered with a net pattern | Sweet and juicy | Wet from the rain | Placed on a high shelf
exam: Ravi netted the ball past the keeper. What does netted mean here? | Hid the ball | Dropped the ball | *Scored a goal | Kicked the ball out of play
